{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791366961,"nonce":"qAHht4NFc/7AQ0cHmbhleDwoqX0=","title":"Rayzor defines static but omits the target.static alias","message":"PreprocessorConfig::default declares Rayzor a statically typed native target and defines static, but not target.static. TestOps has three methods and its boolean constants inside #if target.static. The conformance runner conservatively discovers those method names and injects calls, while the compiler strips the declarations and emits trap placeholders. After metadata precedence is fixed, TestOps reaches the absent testNullOps method and aborts. /tmp/rayzor-metadata-precedence-final-v1/logs/TestOps.log and post-merge MIR establish the missing body.\n\nA copy of the staged project in /tmp/rayzor-target-static-probe adds [build.defines] \"target.static\"=true. It compiles the real method and exposes the separate nullable unary complement crash; this is not an assertion-discovery/scoring change. Define target.static alongside the existing static flag so both spellings select the target's existing semantics. NullableUnaryArithmetic.hx checks this alias only under #if rayzor and shares its arithmetic assertions with native Haxe.","files":null}]}